{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold \"stitch\" task (#5408) to implement the `date` utility for the go-unix-utils project. The specific scope is requirements R1.1 through R1.4 from srd060-date.yaml, covering default behavior and format string support. Two files must be created: `cmd/date/main.go` (the utility implementation) and `cmd/date/date_test.go` (differential tests against gdate). The task must follow strict execution constitution rules including no git commands, writing all files before building, 40-line function limit, and specific coding standards.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: Go binary vs GNU reference binary (gdate) using pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests\n   - SIGPIPE handling: All cmd/ utilities must call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at start of main\n   - strftime-style format string conversion from GNU date format specs to Go time formatting\n   - GNU date padding modifiers: %-d (no padding), %_d (space padding), %0d (zero padding)\n   - GNU extension %P (lowercase am/pm) and %N (nanoseconds)\n   - Standard strftime specs: %Y, %m, %d, %H, %M, %S, %Z, %s, %N, %A, %B, %j, %u, %w\n   - BuildBinary pattern from pkg/testutils for compiling test binaries\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for deterministic test output\n   - Copyright header: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd060-date.yaml` (READ)\n     - This is the SRD defining all requirements for cmd/date\n     - R1.1: No arguments → print current date/time in default format, exit 0\n     - R1.2: +FORMAT argument → strftime-style format string output with newline\n     - R1.3: Standard strftime conversions: %Y, %m, %d, %H, %M, %S, %Z, %s, %N, %A, %B, %j, %u, %w\n     - R1.4: GNU extensions: %P (lowercase am/pm), padding modifiers (%-d no pad, %_d space pad, %0d zero pad)\n     - Non-goals: No -s/--set, no --rfc-3339/--rfc-email, no relative date strings (\"yesterday\", \"2 days ago\")\n     - R2 (date parsing -d), R3 (UTC/reference), R4 (exit codes/testing) exist but are NOT in scope for this task\n\n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (PROVIDED in project_context)\n     - Exports InstallSIGPIPEHandler() which must be called at start of main\n     - Pattern: buffered channel, signal.Notify, goroutine exits process on SIGPIPE\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (PROVIDED in project_context)\n     - DiffTest struct with Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n     - RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests) runs all test cases\n     - BuildBinary(t, \".\") compiles the cmd/ package\n     - buildEnv sets LC_ALL=C by default\n\n   - `cmd/date/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Must implement R1.1-R1.4 only\n     - Must call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n     - Must handle +FORMAT argument parsing\n     - Must convert strftime format specs to Go time format\n\n   - `cmd/date/date_test.go` (TO CREATE)\n     - Must use differential testing against gdate\n     - Must use exec.LookPath(\"gdate\") with t.Skip\n     - Must cover R1.1-R1.4 functionality\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. The SRD was read successfully. Implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the R1.1-R1.4 requirements before implementation\n   - The core challenge will be converting strftime format specifiers to Go's time.Format() reference time approach, since Go uses reference time \"Mon Jan 2 15:04:05 MST 2006\" rather than %Y/%m/%d tokens\n   - GNU padding modifiers (%-d, %_d, %0d) will require custom format string parsing and output manipulation\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely detailed stitch task prompt with full project context, execution constitution, go style constitution, task description specifying creation of cmd/date/main.go and cmd/date/date_test.go implementing srd060 R1.1-R1.4\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of conversation so far\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/date/main.go` implementing R1.1-R1.4 (default date output, +FORMAT parsing, strftime conversion including %Y/%m/%d/%H/%M/%S/%Z/%s/%N/%A/%B/%j/%u/%w, GNU extensions %P and padding modifiers)\n   - Create `cmd/date/date_test.go` with differential tests against gdate covering R1.1-R1.4\n   - Verify compilation: `go vet ./cmd/date/...`\n   - Build binary: `go build -o bin/date ./cmd/date/`\n   - Run tests: `go test ./cmd/date/... -count=1`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd060-date.yaml` and was about to begin implementation. The SRD was the only required_reading file not already provided inline. I now have all the information needed to implement both files. The next step would be to write both `cmd/date/main.go` and `cmd/date/date_test.go` in full before running any build commands, per the implementation strategy in go_style_constitution.\n\n   Key implementation considerations noted:\n   - Scope is ONLY R1.1-R1.4 (this task title: \"[stitch] cmd/date: srd060 R1.1-R1.4\")\n   - Must convert strftime format specifiers to Go time formatting (Go uses reference time pattern not % tokens)\n   - Must handle GNU padding modifiers by parsing the format string character by character\n   - The default GNU date format (no +FORMAT) is like \"Thu Jan  2 15:04:05 MST 2006\"\n   - Tests should use `-d @EPOCH` for deterministic output, but -d is R2 scope - tests for R1.1-R1.4 specifically may need to use env vars like TZ or normalizers for time-dependent output\n   - Note: Since this task is R1.1-R1.4 only (format strings), but the test accept